"$\\mathfrak{sl}(2)$-weight system does not extend to a graph 4-invariant (https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24217)\nciteturn2academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Lando asks whether the $\\mathfrak{sl}(2)$-weight system extends to a unique 4-invariant of graphs.\nTitle: $\\mathfrak{sl}(2)$-weight system does not extend to a graph 4-invariant\nAuthors: Daniil Fomichev, Maksim Karev, Fedor Pavutnitskiy, Sergey Usanov\nDate: Mon Jul 27 09:48:48 2026\n\nA long-standing question by S. Lando asks whether the $\\mathfrak{sl}(2)$-weight system extends to a unique 4-invariant of graphs. We show that, in full generality, the answer to this question is negative. However, for certain specializations of the weight system, extensions do exist. Explicit formulae for computing two such specializations of the weight system are already known. We construct recurrence relations for one additional such extension and discuss the last remaining specialization, which conjecturally admits an extension. We also study the polynomial coefficients of the $\\mathfrak{sl}(2)$-weight system and resolve the questions concerning their extension.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProof of a conjecture of Fomichev and Karev - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0195669826000338)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; Krasilnikov [6] showed that for all graphs with up to 8 vertices such an extension exists and is unique, thus answering in affirmative to Lando’s conjecture for small graphs. ... Since \\psi is also a 4-invariant, Fomichev and Karev, motivated by Lando’s conjecture, proposed the following:\nIndeed, one can associate a weight system to any metrised Lie algebra, as well as to any metrised Lie superalgebra [1], [2], [5].\n\nTo each chord diagram, one can associate a graph, called the intersection graph of the chord diagram. Chmutov and Lando [3] showed that the value of the weight system constructed from the Lie algebra \\mathfrak{sl}\\left(2\\right) on a chord diagram depends only on the intersection graph of the chord diagram, rather than the chord diagram itself. This reveals a deep graph-theoretic facet of the invariant. Lando [7] introduced 4-term relations for graphs and defined the invariants satisfying them as 4-invariants. He showed that any 4-invariant determines a weight system and, consequently by Kontsevich’s theorem, a knot invariant. He then posed the following conjecture:\n\nConjecture 1.1 Lando\n\nThere exists a unique 4-invariant that extends the \\mathfrak{sl}\\left(2\\right)-weight system.\n\nKrasilnikov [6] showed that for all graphs with up to 8 vertices such an extension exists and is unique, thus answering in affirmative to Lando’s conjecture for small graphs.\nIt is known (see, e.g., [2]) that this value of c corresponds to the specialisation of the universal \\mathfrak{sl}\\left(2\\right)-weight system to the 2-dimensional irreducible representation of \\mathfrak{sl}\\left(2\\right). Furthermore, the value of this specialisation on intersection graphs has an explicit formula, which extends to all graphs and is denoted by \\psi  [4], as follows:\n\nDefinition 1.3\n\nFor G\\in \\mathbf{G}, we define \\psi \\left(G\\right)=\\frac{1}{{2}^{2\\left|V\\left(G\\right)\\right|}}\\sum _{U\\subset V\\left(G\\right)}{\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{\\left|V\\left(G\\right)\\right|-\\left|U\\right|}{2}^{corank\\left(A\\left(G{|}_{U}\\right)\\right)},where\n\n  * •\n\nthe sum is taken over all possible subsets U of the vertex set V\\left(G\\right);\n\n  * •\n\nG{|}_{U} is the subgraph of G induced by vertex subset U;\n\n  * •\n\nA\\left(G\\right) is the adjacency matrix of G with coefficients in the field with two elements;\n\n  * •\n\ncorank is the corank of the matrix.\n\nSince \\psi is also a 4-invariant, Fomichev and Karev, motivated by Lando’s conjecture, proposed the following:\n\nConjecture 1.4 [4]\n\nFor G\\in \\mathbf{G}, we have \\phi \\left(G\\right)=\\psi \\left(G\\right).\n\nIn this paper, we prove Conjecture 1.4, thereby verifying an instance of Lando’s conjecture for the specialisation at c=3/8.\n\n## Section snippets\n\n## Proof of Conjecture 1.4\n\nLet G\\in \\mathbf{G}. For a subset U\\subset V\\left(G\\right), we denote by E(U,V\\left(G\\right)\\setminus U) the set of edges with one endpoint in U and the other in V\\left(G\\right)\\setminus U. A graph is Eulerian if all vertex degrees are even. Unlike the standard definition, we do not require Eulerian graphs to be connected.\n\nLemma 2.1\n\n## [4], Proposition 4.1\n\nFor a graph G\\in \\mathbf{G} with the set of vertices V\\left(G\\right) and the set of edges E\\left(G\\right), we have \\phi \\left(G\\right)={2}^{-3\\left|V\\left(G\\right)\\right|}\\sum _{\\genfrac{}{}{0ex}{}{U\\subset V\\left(G\\right)}{G{|}_{U}\\text{ is Eulerian}}}{(-1)}^{\\left|E(U,V\\left(G\\right)\\setminus U)\\right|}{2}^{\\left|U\\right|}.\n\nProof of Conjecture 1.4\n\nWe begin with the definition of \\psi : \\psi \\left(G\\right)={2}^{-2\\left|V\\left(G\\right)\\right|}\\sum _{U\\subset V\\left(G\\right)}{\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}^{\\left|V\\left(G\\right)\\right|-\\left|U\\right|}{2}^{corank\\left(A\\left(G{|}_{U}\\right)\\right)}.Since {2}^{corank\\left(A\\left(G{|}_{U}\\right)\\right)}=\n\n## Acknowledgments\n\nWe sincerely thank the anonymous reviewers for their suggestions, which greatly improved the quality of the presentation of the paper. This work is supported by National Natural Science Foundation of China (Nos. 12471326, 12571379) and 111 Project (No. D23017).\n\n## References (8)\n\n  * D. Bar-Natan\n\n### On the vassiliev knot invariants\n\n### Topology\n\n(1995)\n\n  * D. Fomichev et al.\n\n### The \\mathfrak{sl}(2)-weight system at c=3/8 for graphs\n\n### European J. Combin.\n\n(2025)\n\n  * S. Lando\n\n### On a Hopf algebra in graph theory\n\n### J. Combin. Theory Ser. B\n\n(2000)\n\n  * S. Chmutov et al.\n\n### Introduction to 